You are working on Pigeon, an iOS BLE mesh messaging app.

# Project

Pigeon sends encrypted text messages between iPhones over Bluetooth Low Energy with no internet or server. Each device is both a BLE Central (scanner) and Peripheral (advertiser), forming a mesh network. Messages hop through relay devices. End-to-end encrypted with Curve25519 + AES-256-GCM.

# Build

cd Pigeon && xcodebuild -scheme Pigeon -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17 Pro' build

BLE only works on physical devices, not simulators.

# Stack

Swift 5.9+, SwiftUI, iOS 26.0+, CoreBluetooth, CryptoKit, SwiftData. Zero external dependencies. MVVM with @Observable.

# Critical: Strict Concurrency

SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor. All types are @MainActor by default. When creating value types used across isolation boundaries, mark them `nonisolated` and `Sendable`. The MeshRouter is a Swift `actor`. BLEManager is NSObject with a DispatchQueue. BLEManagerDelegate methods are `nonisolated`.

# Architecture

- AppCoordinator (@Observable, @MainActor): owns all services, injected via .environment()
- BLEManager (NSObject): dual Central+Peripheral, runs on dedicated bleQueue
- MeshRouter (actor): outbound queue per recipient, store-and-forward, dedup cache
- CryptoManager (nonisolated struct): Curve25519 ECDH → HKDF → AES-GCM
- PigeonStore (@MainActor): SwiftData CRUD, maps DTO structs ↔ @Model classes

# Two-Layer Models (IMPORTANT)

DTOs (Message, Peer, Conversation, MessageEnvelope) are nonisolated Codable Sendable structs for networking and crypto. @Model classes (StoredMessage, StoredConversation, StoredPeer) are for SwiftData persistence only. PigeonStore converts between them. NEVER add @Model to DTO structs. NEVER use @Model classes outside PigeonStore.

# Style

- Dark theme via PigeonTheme enum. Background #0A0A0A, accent #8B5CF6. Never hardcode colors.
- Views access coordinator with: @Environment(AppCoordinator.self) private var coordinator
- BLEManager properties accessed by delegate extensions in other files must NOT be private
- BLE messages chunked via MessageProtocol (480-byte payloads, 22-byte binary headers)

# Source Layout

Pigeon/Pigeon/
  PigeonApp.swift, Models/ (4 DTOs), Networking/ (7 BLE+mesh files),
  Crypto/ (2 encrypt files), Persistence/ (4 SwiftData files),
  Services/ (AppCoordinator + NotificationManager), Views/ (11 SwiftUI views)

# Do NOT Build

Group chats, voice/media, read receipts, cloud/server, LoRa, web/Android.
